      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:3652b9788bbdfa1293893bda4e5b67e8f2a72e30261981d05a7113e0765b4075",
      "text": "Shared Case alerting needs recipient authorization beyond collector access. Salesforce CDC ignores record sharing while checking the subscribed user\u2019s field permissions; event schemas can expose field names beyond those permissions. The proposed alert service should check each recipient\u2019s Case access before fan-out and when reading alert history or details. Apache Superset provides a useful precedent for keeping shared broadcasts free of sensitive state. OWASP and a realtime revocation advisory support separate handling of long-lived connection expiry, authorization, and payload redaction. These application design recommendations are distinguished from documented Salesforce behavior.",
